From 6b869770389bd85e4cc7ab23053c49fddfb0b1cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Traveligion <137474479+traveligion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:44:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] chore(deps): update vulnerable dependencies shipped in
 the desktop app

Problem

`npm audit --omit=dev` in frontend/ reports 7 vulnerable packages in the
production dependency tree, i.e. code that is bundled into the packaged
desktop app (1 critical, 2 high, 1 moderate, 3 low):

- seroval 1.5.4 (via @tanstack/router-core): GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c (critical),
  GHSA-jp82-f5mq-hwhp (high)
- js-yaml 4.2.0 (via electron-updater, which parses update metadata):
  GHSA-52cp-r559-cp3m, GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj, GHSA-2883-xcg3-v3hh (high, CPU DoS)
- brace-expansion (high, DoS)
- fflate 0.4.8 (via posthog-js): GHSA-px8p-9vwx-vf98 (moderate)
- dompurify 3.4.14 (direct; also used by mermaid and posthog-js):
  GHSA-p98j-92pf-mc4p, GHSA-6688-9rhm-gjv2 (low, IN_PLACE mode)
- katex 0.16.47 (via mermaid): GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7 (low)

Most of these are not obviously reachable with attacker-controlled input
in this app, but they are cheap to fix without major-version bumps.

Changes

- dompurify: 3.4.14 -> 3.4.16.
- npm overrides: js-yaml ^4.3.2 (resolves to 4.3.2) and katex ^0.18.2
  (resolves to 0.18.10). The latest mermaid release still declares
  katex ^0.16, so an override is the only non-major way to get the fix.
- `npm audit fix` (without --force) in frontend/, packages/product-ui/ and
  packages/cloud-client/, which moves seroval, fflate, brace-expansion,
  undici, @xmldom/xmldom and other transitive packages to patched versions
  within their declared ranges.

Result

- frontend: `npm audit --omit=dev` 7 -> 0 vulnerable packages.
- packages/product-ui and packages/cloud-client: `npm audit` -> 0.
- The remaining frontend findings are build-time only (Electron Forge
  toolchain: tar, tmp, @electron/rebuild, ...) and need Forge 8.

Tested on Linux x64: typecheck, typecheck:e2e, vitest, product-ui and
cloud-client tests, `electron-forge package`, deb maker, app launch.
Mermaid math (KaTeX) rendering was not checked manually.
