From d046f751eb03794d0ab06887b923d2f56874749e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Traveligion <137474479+traveligion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:44:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] chore(electron): upgrade Electron from 33.4.11
 (end-of-life) to 44.7.0

Problem

The desktop app ships Electron 33.4.11 (confirmed in the v0.13.5 .deb).
Electron 33 reached end-of-life on 2025-04-28 and no longer receives
security fixes. As of 2026-10-08, `npm audit` lists 38 advisories against
electron 33.4.11 (11 high, 21 moderate, 6 low).

One of them applies directly to this app's design:
GHSA-v3j7-r9gq-3gjw ("Custom protocol with supportFetchAPI but not
corsEnabled allows cross-origin reads", high, fixed in 39.8.10, 40.9.3,
41.4.0 and 42.0.0). The renderer is served from `app://` registered with
`supportFetchAPI: true` and without `corsEnabled`. On affected versions a
page from another origin in the same session can fetch() `app://` URLs
and read the response. Reproduced with a minimal Electron app: on 33.4.11
a page on http://127.0.0.1 reads the body; on 44.7.0 the fetch is blocked
and the protocol handler is never invoked.
https://github.com/electron/electron/security/advisories/GHSA-v3j7-r9gq-3gjw

Electron 44 is the newest supported major (EOL 2027-03-02).

Changes

- electron: ^33.0.0 -> ^44.7.0.
- Clipboard: Electron 44 rearchitected the clipboard module into an async,
  W3C-style API (see Electron's breaking-changes doc, 44.0).
  - `clipboard.writeText(text, "selection")` is replaced by
    `clipboard.selection.writeText(text)`; both writes are awaited.
  - `clipboard.writeImage()` was removed. The browser view host keeps its
    narrow `writeImage(image)` dependency, and main.ts adapts it to
    `clipboard.write([new ClipboardItem({ "image/png": Blob })])`, so the
    existing unit-test fakes keep working.
- `app.dock` is typed as optional in Electron 44: use `app.dock?.setIcon()`.
- Drop the `allowScripts` entry for electron@33.4.11. Since Electron 42 the
  npm package has no postinstall script: the binary is downloaded on first
  run or explicitly with `npx install-electron`.
- Refresh node-abi in package-lock.json so @electron/rebuild (used by the
  prePackage hook to rebuild better-sqlite3) recognises Electron 44.
  Without this, `electron-forge package` fails with
  "Could not detect abi for version 44.7.0 and runtime electron".

Other breaking changes between 34 and 44 were reviewed against the code
(clearStorageData quotas, plugin-crashed, getBitmap, showHiddenFiles,
ELECTRON_OZONE_PLATFORM_HINT, renderer clipboard access, ...): no other
usages found. The positional `console-message` event arguments used in
browser-view-host.ts are deprecated (since 35) but still work.

Tested on Linux x64: typecheck, typecheck:e2e, vitest, `electron-forge
package`, deb maker; better-sqlite3 loads from the packaged app
(NODE_MODULE_VERSION 149); the app launches under Xvfb, renders the home
screen and starts the bundled daemon. Not tested: macOS (Squirrel.Mac
updater, signing, notarization), Windows, copying a screenshot to the
clipboard through the UI.
