From 9a778a85366727d338218852383e00b64b670b46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Traveligion <137474479+traveligion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:44:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] build(electron): harden the packaged binary with Electron
 fuses

Problem

The released binary keeps every security-relevant fuse at Electron's
permissive default. `npx @electron/fuses read` on the v0.13.5 .deb:

  RunAsNode is Enabled
  EnableCookieEncryption is Disabled
  EnableNodeOptionsEnvironmentVariable is Enabled
  EnableNodeCliInspectArguments is Enabled
  EnableEmbeddedAsarIntegrityValidation is Disabled
  OnlyLoadAppFromAsar is Disabled
  LoadBrowserProcessSpecificV8Snapshot is Disabled
  GrantFileProtocolExtraPrivileges is Enabled

With RunAsNode enabled, `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1 agent-orchestrator -e ...`
turns the app binary into a general-purpose Node.js interpreter
(verified on 0.13.5: it prints Node v20.18.3). Together with NODE_OPTIONS
and --inspect, this lets other local code run under the app's identity and
inherit any OS-level trust or permissions granted to it. Electron
recommends disabling these fuses for apps that do not need them:
https://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/tutorial/fuses

Changes

Add @electron-forge/plugin-fuses 7.11.2 (same version as the rest of Forge)
and @electron/fuses 1.8.0, and flip at package time:

- RunAsNode: false
- EnableNodeOptionsEnvironmentVariable: false
- EnableNodeCliInspectArguments: false
- EnableEmbeddedAsarIntegrityValidation: true
- OnlyLoadAppFromAsar: true
- GrantFileProtocolExtraPrivileges: false

The app does not use ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE, NODE_OPTIONS, --inspect,
child_process.fork or utilityProcess (checked with git grep), and the ACP
runtime ships its own Node binary. `electron-forge start` and the
Playwright e2e launch the unfused node_modules/electron binary, so they
are not affected. For unsigned macOS arm64 builds the Forge plugin resets
the ad-hoc signature after flipping fuses.

Tested on Linux x64: `npx @electron/fuses read` on out/ and on the built
.deb shows the values above; `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1` no longer drops into
Node; the app launches normally, renders the home screen and starts the
daemon. Not tested: macOS and Windows. ASAR integrity validation is only
enforced on macOS and Windows, so it is a no-op on Linux and needs
validation with the signed macOS and Windows builds.
---
 frontend/forge.config.ts   | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 frontend/package-lock.json | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 frontend/package.json      |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+)

